	(text "24 V INPUT PROTECTION\nOrder: fuse -> high-side P-FET (reverse block) -> TVS -> bulk.\nFET drain faces the supply; nothing in the ground path (I2C between boards references GND).\nPass-through to the next board taps +24V_RAW upstream of F2: each board fuses only its own load.\nSMAJ26A clamps at 42.1 V worst case: below the LM317 40 V in-out limit with 3.3 V out,\nand inside the 60 V rating of both bucks."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "459b9f2b-1977-5c3e-a87c-d2a9fdc40495")
	)
	(text "J3 (header, right edge) / J4 (socket, left edge):\ndaisy chain, mate board-to-board. Symmetric pinout:\nreversal maps 24 V to 24 V, GND to GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "65777a26-8832-519a-8fd1-1837e399b9c4")
	)
	(text "J10: 24 V screw terminal (Rev B). Feeds +24V_RAW like J3/J4:\nwire one board, the chain carries the rest."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50 108 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "51b50153-e96b-5596-bbe6-2bc72b0e453b")
	)
	(text "+5V BUCK (Raspberry Pi, 5 A)\nTPS54560B: 60 V, 5 A, Eco-mode pulse skipping at light load:\nboards 2 and 3 run it unloaded. fsw = 400 kHz (RT 243k).\nVout = 0.8 V x (1 + 53.6k/10k) = 5.09 V.\nCOMPENSATION VALUES ARE A STARTING POINT: re-derive in TI WEBENCH for the final L/Cout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 125 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d7627de1-e51d-5a4e-9204-c466cba7877c")
	)
	(text "EN left open: internal pull-up enables the part."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 195 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e3815ae-3a1b-5fb9-84bf-1f06d4eb1352")
	)
	(text "+3.3V BUCK (4x FT4232H, hub, 8x MAX3232E: ~700 mA)\nTPS54360B: 60 V, 3.5 A, Eco-mode. fsw = 400 kHz.\nVout = 0.8 V x (1 + 31.6k/10k) = 3.33 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220 125 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "87f16bef-9481-5ea1-af7b-49c66a3c96c1")
	)
	(text "BRING-UP HEADERS (Rev B)\n1 = supply, 2 = section, 3 = GND. Jumper 1-2 = normal.\nOff = section unpowered; meter across 1-2 = current;\nbench supply on 2-3 = feed the section alone.\nA jumper on 2-3 only grounds the dead section."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118 140 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d38f3a5-96d2-5947-8f12-2cdda2f8d327")
	)
	(text "RAIL CURRENT SENSE (Rev B)\nINA219 on INA_SDA/INA_SCL (MCU bus, powered from +3V3_MCU).\nU23 0x40: 5 mOhm on +5V (25 mV at 5 A). U24 0x41: 10 mOhm on +3.3V.\nBuck feedback is taken BEFORE the shunt; Kelvin IN+/IN- from the shunt pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 318 134 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5c5c3211-a1ff-5e00-a943-52759114a87f")
	)
	(text "RAIL LEDs (Rev B), green, ~1 mA: on = rail present."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 100 234 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "40c6b32d-5105-59f5-affe-aa57ec5d7361")
	)
	(text "+3V3_MCU: independent LM317 off +24V, so the MCU outlives the rails it monitors.\nR9 = 240R sets 5.2 mA minimum load - do not raise it. Vout = 1.25 x (1 + 390/240) = 3.28 V.\nDissipation ~315 mW. SOT-223 tab is the OUTPUT (3.3 V pour), not GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "acfe58aa-7179-5832-8525-d5f7789f1d57")
	)
	(text "TEST POINTS - rails"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23 261 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3e1c0bb0-0905-5f83-a067-d8af7492b5cf")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
